WHAT THIS LICENSE COVERS

This license applies to the *compiled work*: the harmonisation of 1,010 raw
report columns into 863 canonical indicators, the data dictionary, the
verification and repair scripts, the documentation (README, CODEBOOK), and the
interactive Data Explorer (index.html and its assets).

UNDERLYING SOURCE DATA

The underlying facility and workforce figures are drawn from the Rural Health
Statistics annual reports published by the Ministry of Health & Family Welfare,
Government of India (2005 to 2022-23). Those source figures are Government of
India material; this project claims no rights over them and redistributes them
for research and public-interest use. Base-map geometry is derived from Census
of India 2011 district boundaries (DataMeet community maps, CC BY).

HOW TO CITE

  Association for Socially Applicable Research (ASAR). Rural Health Statistics
  of India — harmonised dataset, 2005–2023. Compiled from Ministry of Health &
  Family Welfare, Rural Health Statistics annual reports. Version 1.0, 2026.
  https://asarforindia.github.io/rhs-india/

For policy or academic use, figures should be cross-checked against the
original Rural Health Statistics report of the relevant year.

NO WARRANTY

This is an independent research compilation, not an official publication of the
Ministry of Health & Family Welfare. The material is provided "as is", without
warranty of any kind.
